            "title": "More Bonds Are Teetering on the Brink of Junk: Credit Weekly",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The first full week of the year has been one of the busiest for US corporate debt sales on record, and risk premiums stayed low even amid heavy issuance.  Around $63 billion of US corporate bonds in the high-grade universe have a high-yield rating from one bond grader, a BBB- rating from others, and at least one negative outlook, according to the bank\u2019s review based on ratings for debt in its high-grade US index.  \u201cAs companies continue to refinance debt, the pressure on their balance sheets from rising interest expense is growing,\u201d said Nathaniel Rosenbaum, a US high-grade credit strategist at JPMorgan.",
